{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: tested whether playoff defenses change scheme, using scheme labels inferred backwards from opponent play-type PPP (523 within-game cells, 440 game pairs). Transition matrices were near-uniform, consistent with label noise. Applies to analyses that use these outcome-inferred scheme labels, which cannot separate a defensive change from the offense executing differently. Does not record an error rate for directly observed labels.", "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-005 | Study family SF-APPA-005: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)\n- observed_research_question: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Playoff defenses change scheme within games and between games, especially after the opponent ran a play type heavily.\n- observed_result: Within-game change 319/523 (61.0%); cross-game change 298/440 (67.7%); 103/104 units (99.0%) and 52/52 series show a change; transition matrices near-uniform.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- observed_failure_evidence: Doc caveat: inferred label cannot separate real defensive adjustment from offense executing differently; near-uniform transition matrices consistent with label noise.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 523 cells; 440 pairs\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-030", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: verified the backfilled play-type labels (921,514 possessions) against league bands and team identities. The verification failed: PNR share 28.7% (band 20-28%), PULL_UP 7.9%, near 0% for many 2024-25 teams, 82.8% of PNR labels proxy-calibrated. Applies to analyses using these backfilled labels, PNR and PULL_UP most directly. Does not record how much the failures bias any particular estimate.", "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-030 | Study family SF-APPA-030: Play-type label backfill verification\n- observed_research_question: Play-type label backfill verification\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Backfilled play-type labels match expected league distributions and team identities.\n- observed_result: PNR 28.7% FAIL (band 20-28%); PULL_UP 7.9% FAIL; 3100 games with team PNR >33% FAIL; PNR PPP 0.948 PASS; temporal PASS; team identity FAIL; 2024-25 PULL_UP ~0-1% for many teams. Final: FAIL.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- observed_failure_evidence: 2024-25 PULL_UP shares 0.0-2.0% for many teams; 82.8% of PNR labels proxy_calibrated.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 921,514 possessions\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPA-001\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPA-005"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-058", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: one game (0042500101) tested whether NBA matchup and play-by-play fields can label on-ball coverage (DROP, ICE, SWITCH). Only 14.9% and 3.3% of on-ball possessions got a confident label, and the switch field was not populated. Applies to analyses that need observed coverage labels from these feeds. Does not record results from tracking data or from more games.", "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-058 | Study family SF-APPS-058: Observed on-ball defensive scheme labels (ORL-DET G1)\n- observed_research_question: Observed on-ball defensive scheme labels (ORL-DET G1)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: NBA matchup/PBP fields can label on-ball coverage (DROP/ICE/SWITCH) at usable rates.\n- observed_result: DET: 67 on-ball HC poss, 10 labeled (14.9%) ? DROP n=5 PPP=1.20, ICE_CANDIDATE n=5 PPP=0.80, OTHER n=57 PPP=1.42. ORL: 60 poss, 2 labeled (3.3%). switches_on unpopulated.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Confident label rates 14.9% and 3.3%; NBA matchups feed did not populate switches_on.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=67/60 possessions, 10/2 labeled\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: failed_gate"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-025", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: audited play-type labels for foul leakage. 36% of OTHER possessions end in fouls, inflating OTHER PPP; DRIVE sits 12 points below the foul benchmark; PNR shows a 22% foul rate; initiation_type maps only 335 of 50,668 possessions (0.7%) to a play type. Applies to analyses whose result depends on PPP differences between play types, OTHER and DRIVE most directly, or on initiation_type. Does not record label error for other categories or the bias in any downstream estimate.", "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-025 | Study family SF-CHT-025: Play-type labeling audit: OTHER/DRIVE foul leakage\n- observed_research_question: Play-type labeling audit: OTHER/DRIVE foul leakage\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: Play-type PPP differences are real efficiency, not labeling/foul artifacts.\n- observed_result: OTHER: 36% end in fouls, PPP inflated (FOUL_BUCKET). DRIVE: 12pp below foul benchmark (FOUL_LEAK). PNR shows 22% foul rate. Only 335 of 50,668 possessions (0.7%) map to a real play type via initiation_type.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- observed_failure_evidence: OTHER PPP inflated by 36% foul endings; DRIVE 12pp below foul benchmark; initiation_type maps 0.7%.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 50,668 possessions in the initiation_type check\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Per-PT diagnostic of foul-ending share vs PPP; initiation_type mapping.\n- observed_verdict: artifact_found"}], "n_results": 4}

